    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a1-a31">

                <pb facs="0414" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg356"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San Juan Bautista</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 2,1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>V<hi rendition="#small-caps">ery Distinguished and Esteemed Sir</hi>: Your two
                    acceptable letters reached me the 27th of October and 9th of November last.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I will have the decrees Mr. Romero sent me published to-morrow, and with great
                    pleasure, for the whole State approves of them as well as myself. There is no
                    man of greater merit than you in the nation, nor one who has given more hope by
                    taking the supreme command at a time when constant changes created great
                    distrust. The trial of Ortega is a fact that gives influence to the government
                    from the morality it infuses into our society, and especially among our great
                    men, accustomed to stand upon their dignity for protection, for it makes their
                    offences more serious.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. MENDEZ.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benito Juarez, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >President of the Republic, Chihuahua</hi></hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
